From 4a5b6c7d8e9f0a1b2c3d4e5f60718293a4b5c6d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: noname <noname@example.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0032 answer the pop-up the cloud game opens behind, with an enter of its own

GeForce NOW puts a pop-up in front of the game before it starts: Steam's own
notice, which only an Enter dismisses. Measured on this board over the two
Destiny 2 sessions: the window takes the seat keyboard and answers Enter
(the stream window logged wayland-video input: key 28 vk=0xd pressed=1 twice
at 07:38:06, and the ydotoold jiggle run logged 20 forwards of it at 09:12-09:14
while the picture held fps=48.7 committed=13125 dropped=0), so the key that is
sent does reach the host - but the pop-up appears some way into the cloud boot,
the presses a person makes at the very start of the stream land in front of it,
and a session started while the sofa is empty gets no press at all. It also
shows what makes the keyboard go away: at 07:39:46.984 weston logged event1 -
Dell Dell USB Keyboard: device removed, and 30 ms later the window logged
wayland-video input: capture inactive; in weston's own source that is
weston_seat_release_keyboard(), which answers a device leaving the seat with
weston_keyboard_set_focus(NULL) and cancel_grab, and nothing puts the focus
back until a pointer motion activates the window again (weston_view_activate_input).
So a press made through the compositor is the fragile one. Arm the answer at the
key API instead: the surface already holds the streamer's input hooks, and submitKey
sends the same VK_RETURN a physical Enter becomes, so a clock that calls them needs
nothing from the compositor. OPENNOW_POPUP_ENTER_MS arms it that many ms after the
stream window became live, OPENNOW_POPUP_ENTER_TIMES repeats the press 5 s apart
(4 times when unset), and OPENNOW_POPUP_ENTER_MS unset arms nothing, which leaves
every earlier series' run unchanged. The teardown stops the clock, so a session
that ended cannot press Enter into whatever the interface comes back to.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [STM32MP25 performance work]

